{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533819-need-help-developing-a-meta-discipline","id":1533819,"title":"Need help developing a meta-discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-08T08:43:50-07:00","id":1533819,"title":"Need help developing a meta-discipline","content":"I'm not using 20A rules for this. I am using the Dark Ages: Vampire rules (black book with the red rosary ankh on it). A player wants to create a meta-discipline ie. combo-discipline that will use Vicissitude 5 to reflexively transform a part of his body into blood so that he can avoid taking any damage from an incoming attack. I imagine that it would have to be expensive to develop and taxing to use (perhaps blood + Willpower) and to recover from. Additionally, I would say that this defense would be useless against fire, magic, and sunlight as well as weapons that have been blessed by True Faith individuals. Would this ability use Celerity 5 too? Any other ideas for what it would use? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:04:49-07:00","id":1533823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533819-need-help-developing-a-meta-discipline#post1533819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not using 20A rules for this. I am using the Dark Ages: Vampire rules (black book with the red rosary ankh on it). A player wants to create a meta-discipline ie. combo-discipline that will use Vicissitude 5 to reflexively transform a part of his body into blood so that he can avoid taking any damage from an incoming attack. I imagine that it would have to be expensive to develop and taxing to use (perhaps blood + Willpower) and to recover from. Additionally, I would say that this defense would be useless against fire, magic, and sunlight as well as weapons that have been blessed by True Faith individuals. Would this ability use Celerity 5 too? Any other ideas for what it would use? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you want already exists:<ul><li>Bloodform (A vampire with this power can physically transform all or part of her body into sentient vitae) PLUS</li> <li>Promethean Clay merit (The difficulty to use any Vicissitude power on yourself is two less than normal, and you may activate Vicissitude powers reflexively at your full dice pool while taking other actions).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:11:10-07:00","id":1533824,"title":"","content":"The problem is that he already made his charcater and can't take anymore merits. This is an established charcater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T03:57:04-07:00","id":1533949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533819-need-help-developing-a-meta-discipline?p=1533823#post1533823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you want already exists:<ul><li>Bloodform (A vampire with this power can physically transform all or part of her body into sentient vitae) PLUS</li> <li>Promethean Clay merit (The difficulty to use any Vicissitude power on yourself is two less than normal, and you may activate Vicissitude powers reflexively at your full dice pool while taking other actions).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on edition (blood form is different in basically every edition), Promethean Clay isn't even necessary. One of the editions' versions of it allows this as-written -- and I'm pretty sure it's revised DA:V, since VtDA has probably the worst iteration of Vicissitude 5 ever printed and V20 DA:V has Body Impolitic instead.<br /> <br /> At any rate, the rules are same as any other incorporeal transformation at a level 5 iteration (i.e. mist form and shadow form): it doesn't protect against fire, sunlight, magic, or faith. I believe it costs 1 BP per hit taken, to account for the blood &quot;knocked away&quot; when the attack comes in contact. And yes, it is extraordinarily nasty when the player inevitably takes acid blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}